  "notes": "The spec unifies the three list types by unifying their element types, tuples that unify element by element, and the first elements of those tuples, a set of strings, a set of lists of strings and a number, have no common type. The set type of s doesn't help: list and set types unify by preferring the list type, and the dynamic pseudo-type is the result only when every input type is dynamic, so its dynamic elements can't stand for the others. So this should be an error, as converting to a list of any is when the elements have no common type. hashicorp/hcl ranks the given types (compareTypes in cty/convert/compare_types.go) and converts every empty list to s's type, whose dynamic pseudo-type elements take anything. It ranks neither of a string and a list above the other: if it did, the three lists would rank in a circle (each wins at one element), and sortTypes in cty/convert/sort_types.go would never reach s.",
